{"Title":"An Act relative to vehicle warranty fulfillment ","BillNumber":"H321","DocketNumber":"HD522","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"SSH1","Name":"Steven S. Howitt","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SSH1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-11T16:23:34.01"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"SSH1","Name":"Steven S. Howitt","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SSH1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-11T16:23:34.01"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H321/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Howitt of Seekonk, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 321) of Steven S. Howitt relative to warranty for motor vehicles after certain sales.  Consumer Protection and Professional Licensure.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 16 of chapter 90D of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2018 Official Edition, is hereby amended by adding the following subsection:-\r\n\t(c) If an automobile dealer or private individual buys a vehicle and holds it for resale, said dealer or individual shall honor any optional pre-paid manufacturers vehicle warranty plan corresponding to the automobile’s Vehicle Identification Number (VIN) upon resale. Said warranty shall remain valid until the warranty timing and/or mileage agreement is fulfilled.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J17","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J17"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}